            <title>0.25.6</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:40:36 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>53</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.25.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.25.6</h3><ul><li>Setup now has a "Keep Keeploop up to date" switch, on by default. If you never chose, Keeploop asks you once in the menu: Turn On or Not Now. You can change it any time in Settings &gt; General.</li><li>Updates now reach every Mac at once instead of a few Macs a day.</li><li>Claude chats on your Mac now use Keeploop's local connector when it is there and leave Keeploop Remote for the web and your phone. Keeploop no longer suggests switching Keeploop Remote off.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
